1
00:00:00,437 --> 00:00:02,178
(Q31) Good morning.

2
00:00:02,178 --> 00:00:10,468
Now, we’ve been asked to choose an aspect of European clothing or fashion and to talk about its development over time.

3
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:16,536
I decided to focus on a rather small area of clothing and that’s pockets.

4
00:00:16,536 --> 00:00:20,016
I chose pockets for two reasons, really.

5
00:00:20,016 --> 00:00:36,435
[Q31答案句] We all have them – in jeans, jackets, coats, for example – and even though we often carry bags or briefcases as well, nothing is quite as convenient as being able to pop your phone or credit card into your pocket.

6
00:00:36,435 --> 00:00:46,457
Yet, I suspect that, other than that, people don’t really think about pockets too much and they’re rather overlooked as a fashion item.

7
00:00:46,457 --> 00:00:53,543
(Q32) It’s certainly very interesting to go back in time and see how pockets developed for men and women.

8
00:00:53,543 --> 00:01:01,191
In the 18th century, fashions were quite different from the way they are now, and pockets were too.

9
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:08,927
[Q32答案句] If we think about male fashion first … that was the time when suits became popular.

10
00:01:08,927 --> 00:01:28,557
(Q33) [Q33答案句] Trousers were knee-length only and referred to as ‘breeches’, the waistcoats were short and the jackets were long, but all three garments were lined with material and pockets were sewn into this cloth by whichever tailor the customer used.

11
00:01:28,557 --> 00:01:38,623
(Q34) The wearer could then carry small objects such as pencils or coins on their person and reach them through a gap in the lining.

12
00:01:38,623 --> 00:01:58,182
[Q34答案句] Coat pockets became increasingly decorative on the outside for men who wanted to look stylish, but they were often larger but plainer if the wearer was someone with a profession who needed to carry medical instruments – a doctor or physician, for example.

13
00:01:58,182 --> 00:02:04,063
(Q35) The development of women’s pockets was a little different.

14
00:02:04,063 --> 00:02:10,157
[Q35答案句] For one thing, they weren’t nearly as visible or as easy to reach as men’s.

15
00:02:10,157 --> 00:02:20,878
(Q36) In the 18th and 19th centuries, women carried numerous possessions on their person and some of these could be worth a lot of money.

16
00:02:20,878 --> 00:02:29,449
Women were more vulnerable to theft and wealthy women, in particular, worried constantly about pickpockets.

17
00:02:29,449 --> 00:02:36,544
[Q36答案句] So – what they did was to have a pair of pockets made that were tied together with string.

18
00:02:36,544 --> 00:02:50,229
(Q37) The pockets were made of fabric, which might be recycled cloth if the wearer had little money or something more expensive, such as linen, sometimes featuring very delicate embroidery.

19
00:02:50,229 --> 00:02:56,245
[Q37答案句] Women tied the pockets around their waist so that they hung beneath their clothes.

20
00:02:56,245 --> 00:03:07,153
(Q38) Remember, skirts were long then and there was plenty of room to hide a whole range of small possessions between the layers of petticoats that were commonly worn.

21
00:03:07,153 --> 00:03:15,631
[Q38答案句] They would have an opening in the folds of their skirts through which they could reach whatever they needed, like their perfume.

22
00:03:15,631 --> 00:03:36,222
(Q39) Working women, of course, also needed to carry around items that they might use for whatever job or trade they were involved in, but their pairs of pockets still remained on the inside of their clothing, they just got bigger or longer – sometimes reaching down to their knees!

23
00:03:36,222 --> 00:03:47,383
So the tie-on pockets went well into the 19th century and only changed when fashion altered towards the end of that period.

24
00:03:47,383 --> 00:03:59,502
[Q39答案句] That’s when dresses became tighter and less bulky, and the pairs of pockets became very noticeable – they stood out too much and detracted from the woman’s image.

25
00:03:59,502 --> 00:04:10,918
(Q40) Women who had been used to carrying around a range of personal possessions – and still wanted to – needed somewhere to carry these items about their person.

26
00:04:10,918 --> 00:04:13,418
[Q40答案句] That was when small bags, or pouches as they were known, came into fashion and, of course, they inevitably led on to the handbag of more modern times, particularly when fashion removed pockets altogether.

